course: dictionary
lesson: 1108
title: Brave
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Brave means ready to do something difficult or frightening, even though you feel afraid. Being brave does not mean having no fear. The fear is still there, and you do the right thing anyway.
explain: «A shaky voice before a hospital visit means a grown-up is scared; being brave means doing the scary thing anyway, not feeling no fear.» The clue is in the shaky voice: a brave person can still be scared.
explain: Brave is not the same as reckless. Taking silly risks, like climbing onto a roof just to show off, is not brave. A brave person thinks first, then faces the scary thing for a good reason.
fact: Brave means ready to do something difficult or frightening, even though you feel afraid.
fact: To brave something, like bad weather, means to face it and go through it.
fact: «The brave» means brave people, as in old stories.
fact: «Friendships often start with one brave, kind person.» Saying hello to someone who is eating alone can take courage.
fact: Phrases to know: «be brave», «brave enough to», «put on a brave face», «brave the weather».
exercise: Lucy sits down next to Harper, who is eating lunch alone, and asks her to play. Why is this brave? | It means Lucy is good at running fast | *It takes courage to be kind to someone new, even if Lucy feels a little nervous | It means Lucy is the best player at school | It means Lucy is not scared at all
exercise: What does «brave the weather» mean? | Ask the weather to be nice | Stay inside because it is raining | *Face bad weather and go out into it anyway | Wear a big coat for warmth
exercise: In old stories, what does «the brave» mean? | Old castles | Sad songs | Rainy days | *Brave people
test: Which action is brave, not reckless? | Eating ten sweets in a row | Climbing onto a roof to show off | Running across a busy road without looking | *Telling the truth when you have made a mistake, even though you feel nervous
test: «She put on a brave face before the dentist.» What does this mean? | *She tried to look calm even though she was scared | She felt no fear at all | She ran away from the dentist | She was too sleepy to care
exam: Which sentence shows bravery as doing the scary thing anyway, not feeling no fear? | The dog was brave because it was big | Lily felt nothing at all when the bell rang | Harper was never scared of anything at school | *Sam was frightened of the dark, but he walked to his room alone anyway
